{
  "configuration_id": "config_025",
  "reason": "The current best (config_019: PCA-2000, ResNet50, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile; acc=0.639) establishes that multimodal + multiprofile + avgpool + weighted is a strong recipe. However, the image encoder remains the largest source of uncertainty: ResNet50 alone achieved only 0.208 accuracy, yet it contributed ~0.15 on top of RNA-only, suggesting the image signal is underutilized by a weak encoder. Config_025 swaps ResNet50 → ImageNet ViT-L while holding every other hyperparameter identical to config_019, giving a clean A/B test of image encoder quality. If ViT-L yields a meaningful gain, it confirms the image modality has untapped potential and justifies further investment in stronger image representations (and combinations with learned RNA encoders). If it yields little gain, it indicates the image contribution is inherently limited and redirects budget toward RNA encoder upgrades (scvi/scGPT). This single experiment resolves the highest-uncertainty design axis while remaining a direct exploitation of the best-known configuration, making it the most budget-efficient next step."
}

